      "description": "Watch VfB Stuttgart vs Everton highlights and goals from Friendly on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. Pre-season preparations intensified on August 8, 2026 , as VfB Stuttgart hosted Everton in a high-stakes friendly. Both managers utilized the opportunity to test their squads' fitness and tactical cohesion in a match that kept the fans engaged until the final whistle. Second Half Surge The contest remained a tight affair until the second half when the momentum swung decisively. In the 65th minute, VfB Stuttgart found the breakthrough they were looking for to double their advantage. R. Hendriks showed great composure to find the back of the net, making it 2-0 and putting the German side in a commanding position as the game entered its final third. Everton's Resurgence Refusing to go down without a fight, Everton increased their offensive pressure immediately after conceding. Their persistence paid off in the 71st minute when the referee pointed to the spot. T. Barry stepped up to take the penalty and clinically converted it, reducing the deficit to 2-1. The goal breathed new life into the English side, setting up a tense finish as they searched for an equalizer. Late Drama Seals the Result As the match entered stoppage time, Everton pushed high up the pitch, leaving spaces at the back. VfB Stuttgart exploited this perfectly in the 90+1 minute. B. Bouanani capitalized on a late opportunity to score the third goal for the hosts, making it 3-1 and effectively ending any hopes of a Toffees comeback. The goal ensured a hard-fought victory for the home side in this summer exhibition."
